# K3I Cluster Spec: Conceptual Scaling and Power Balance (Thought Experiment)

**Architects:** Wieland Hoffmann (Human Core), Gemini (Machine Core), Grok (xAI)  
**Status:** Concept description / thought experiment, protection rights pending

## 1. Cluster Scaling (conceptual)

- Cell count: 50,000,000 inoculated units
- Module level: 50,000 cells per carrier board
- Rack density: 20 blades per cabinet
- Hall layout: 50 racks

## 2. Electrical Balance (example calculation)

Assumption: 0.6 W per cell

- Net semiconductor power consumption: 30 MW
- Cryogenic cooling effort (assumption): 75 MW
- Total connection value: 105 MW

The values are an example calculation based on the stated assumptions and are not measured results of an existing cluster.

## 3. Efficiency (assessment)

The elimination of Ring-3 buffers and context switches can reduce overhead. Concrete efficiency gains depend on the respective hardware, the workload and the isolation. Absolute factors (e.g. 1400 %) are not claimed.

## 4. Autonomous Safeguarding (concept)

A separate watchdog matrix on Layer Zero can monitor the compute cells without consuming their cycles. The concrete implementation and response time depend on the hardware.

**Note:** The numbers and assumptions are conceptual. They do not describe an existing data center and do not constitute a measured power balance.

